> 
> So, me being level 11, getting a newt is not possible?

Not *im*possible. You'll probably get some mid-level monster like a
rothe or a yeti. If you think it'll be too heavy to carry to the altar,
try to kill it while it's on the altar.

>> > If I kill the priest myself, will Odin kill me?
>>
>> Probably. When I tried in explore mode Odin tried to fry me with a
>> bold 

(that's "bolt", of course)

>> of lightning (and would have succeeded if it hadn't been explore 
>> mode).
> 
> I have reflection, so I'm not scared. As long he only tries once ;)

Hmm, after the lightning comes the wide-angle disintegration beam, IIRC.
Are you disintegration-resistant?

>> > Will my own god be so
>> > pissed that I can't appease him again (say, by saccing that unicorn
>> > I have with me ;) )
>>
>> Don't *ever* sacrifice a unicorn on an altar of its own alignment.
>> And don't sacrifice a unicorn of your own alignment on a
>> cross-aligned altar unless you really *want* to convert yourself.
> 
> But I want to convert it with a newt, can't I do that first?

You want to convert it with anything at all *except* unicorns, your own
species, or corpses that have been dead too long like those from
mummies or zombies. Elves are all right, gnomes, monkeys, and if you
happen to be a lawful *dwarven* Valk, like all of my Valks, even the
priest of Odin himself.

It's probably not wise to do it first, i.e. while the priest is still
alive. Priests are tough, and gods are vengeful.

>> And if you've just killed the priest yourself (not by letting a pet
>> kill him, or with conflict) Tyr will probably be so angry that you
>> won't be able to sacrifice *anything* on Odin's altar without risking
>> converting yourself instead of the altar.
> 
> Lets say, I manage to survive killing the priest, and converting the
> altar with a newt, can I then make up with Tyr somehow?

If you kill the priest you'll have to wait a long time (and/or use an
altar that's already coaligned, but you said you don't have any) to get
in good enough standing with Tyr to even *think* of converting the
altar. If you manage to survive killing the priest, go and do other
things instead until you get a foo of enlightenment that tells you that
you can safely pray; then you can safely try to convert the altar.

